(M1 test B: 2Sigma+ and 2Pi states of one p electron, Hund's case (d).)
(Equal potentials, <L**2>=2 for both states, constant <Pi|L+|Sigma>=sqrt(2),)
(no spin-orbit and no spin-rotation: H = T + V(r) + B(r) R**2, where R is the)
(nuclear rotation. L + g_s S acts on electron coordinates only and commutes)
(with R**2, so M1 joins only degenerate levels of one R. Every M1 line with)
(nonzero frequency must vanish.)
masses 1.0 16.0
molecule fictitious
nstates 2
jrot 0.5 - 3.5
symmetry Cs(M)
grid
  npoints 151
  range  0.55 2.0
  type 0
end
contraction
  vib
  vmax 4 4
end
checkpoint
  eigenfunc save ascii
  filename M1_p_electron_cased
end
poten 1
name "X2Sigma+"
type polynomial
lambda 0
mult 2
symmetry +
units cm-1
values
c0     0.0
re     0.97
c1     0.0
c2 40000.0
end
poten 2
name "A2Pi"
type polynomial
lambda 1
mult 2
units cm-1
values
c0     0.0
re     0.97
c1     0.0
c2 40000.0
end
L2 1
name "<X|L**2|X>"
lambda 0
spin 0.5
type polynomial
values
c0 2.0
end
L2 2
name "<A|L**2|A>"
lambda 1
spin 0.5
type polynomial
values
c0 2.0
end
L+ 2 1
name "<A|L+|X>"
lambda 1 0
spin 0.5 0.5
type polynomial
values
c0 1.4142135623730951
end
intensity
  magdipole
  absorption
  thresh_intes 1e-300
  thresh_line 1e-300
  temperature 300
  gns 1.0 1.0
  J, 0.5, 3.5
  freq-window 0.001, 50000
  energy low -0.001, 50000, upper -0.001, 50000
end
